the new CEO to create a transformation plan\n\nFounded in 1998, Lululemon Athletica is based in Vancouver, Canada, though it is incorporated in Delaware and its financial results are reported in U.S. dollars. The company designs and sells athletic apparel, and markets its yoga-inspired clothing under the lululemon athletica and ivivva athletica brand names. It also sells fitness pants, shorts, tops, and jackets designed for running and other sports. The company has approximately 39,000 employees. The LULU shares are a component of the S&P 500.\n\nArgus• last month \n- ### The Fed meets this week and odds are growing that a rate hike is coming. Last\n\nThe Fed meets this week and odds are growing that a rate hike is coming. Last week, the Dow Jones Industrial Average lost 2%, while the S&P 500 and the Nasdaq Composite each shed 1%. Year to date, all three indices are in positive territory, with the Dow up 9%, the S&P 500 up 12%, and the Nasdaq up 13%. The rate decision from the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) is the main event on Wall Street this week. The Fed's meeting starts on Tuesday and the decision on rates comes on Wednesday afternoon, followed as usual by the chairman's press conference. The odds are now at 87% that there will be a rate hike, this following recent strong jobs data and stubborn inflation news. On the earnings calendar, the volume of reports is light as earnings season is over. In the next few weeks, there will be sporadic reports from the likes of Nike, Costco, Micron Technologies, and FedEx. The next earnings season starts up in mid-October when the big banks begin reporting on October 13. Aside from the Fed meeting, the highest-profile economic release this week is Retail Sales on Wednesday. Turning to economic data, gas prices ticked higher by nine cents last week, to an average of $4.16 per gallon for regular gas. Elsewhere, the Atlanta Fed GDPNow forecast calls for 3Q GDP growth of 4.4%, down a bit from last week. The Cleveland Fed Inflation Nowcast is at 3.4% for September, unchanged from last week. Mortgage rates inched up another five basis points last week, with the average 30-year fixed-rate mortgage now at 6.76%, according to FreddieMac. Taking a deeper dive into performance so far in 2026, a leading industrialized global stock market index, the ETF EFA, is up 11% year to date, while the leading emerging market ETF (EEM) is up 24%. U.S. growth stocks are up 3% when looking at ETF IWF, while value stocks (IWD) are up 21%. Crude oil prices continue to be volatile. On Friday, oil closed at $101 per barrel and is up 73% for the year. In other asset classes for the year to date, AGG bonds are down 4%, gold is flat, and Bitcoin is down 11%. The U.S. dollar is up 1%, tracking DXY. The VIX Volatility Index was about 16 on Friday, below its historical average of 20. Turning to sector performance, the list from first to worst so far in 2026 is Energy (+45%), Information Technology (+29%), Materials (+12%), Industrials (+10%), Healthcare (+7%), Real Estate (+7%), Consumer Staples (+7%), Financials (+4%), Utilities (flat), Communication Services (-5%), and Consumer Discretionary (-6%).\n\nArgus• last month \n- ### Lululemon Relies on Popular Brand and Product Introductions to Counter Tough Competition\n\nLululemon Athletica designs, distributes, and markets athletic apparel, footwear, and accessories for women, men, and girls. The company offers pants, shorts, tops, and jackets for both leisure and athletic activities such as yoga and running. Lululemon also sells fitness accessories, such as bags, yoga mats, and equipment. It sells its products through digital channels, a small number of wholesale partners, more than 800 company-owned stores in about two dozen countries in North America, Asia, and Western Europe, and about 45 franchised locations in the Middle East and Europe. The company was founded in 1998 and is based in Vancouver, Canada. \n\nMorningstar• last month \n- ### Lululemon Earnings: Guidance Cut Highlights Challenges Facing Incoming CEO; Shares Attractive\n\nLululemon Athletica designs, distributes, and markets athletic apparel, footwear, and accessories for women, men, and girls. The company offers pants, shorts, tops, and jackets for both leisure and athletic activities such as yoga and running. Lululemon also sells fitness accessories, such as bags, yoga mats, and equipment. It sells its products through digital channels, a small number of wholesale partners, more than 800 company-owned stores in about two dozen countries in North America, Asia, and Western Europe, and about 45 franchised locations in the Middle East and Europe. The company was founded in 1998 and is based in Vancouver, Canada. \n\nMorningstar• last month","title":"lululemon athletica inc. (LULU) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo Finance","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/LULU/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DECK/","text":"Deckers Outdoor Corporation (DECK) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo Finance\n\n# Deckers Outdoor Corporation (DECK)\n\n81.09 -4.19 (-4.91%)\n\n At close: October 23 at 4:00:03 PM EDT \n\n80.84 -0.25 (-0.30%)\n\nAfter hours: October 23 at 5:51:35 PM EDT\n\n## Trading disclosure\n\n### -5.39%\n\n### 3.18%\n\n### -24.71%\n\n### -21.78%\n\n### -20.92%\n\n### 28.35%\n\nDECK\n\nAnalyst Rating\n\nDate Oct 23, 2026\n\nAnalyst Needham\n\nRating Action Maintains\n\nRating Buy\n\nPrice Action Lowers \n\nPrice Target 125 -> 96 \n\nAnalyst Rating\n\nDate Oct 23, 2026\n\nAnalyst Stifel\n\nRating Action Maintains\n\nPrice Action Lowers \n\nPrice Target 133 -> 113 \n\nAnalyst Rating\n\nDate Oct 23, 2026\n\nAnalyst Wells Fargo\n\nRating Action Maintains\n\nRating Underweight\n\nPrice Action Lowers \n\nPrice Target 85 -> 70 \n\nAnalyst Rating\n\nDate Oct 23, 2026\n\nPrice Action Lowers \n\nPrice Target 90 -> 84 \n\nAnalyst Rating\n\nDate Oct 23, 2026\n\nPrice Action Lowers \n\nPrice Target 105 -> 95 \n\nAnalyst Rating\n\nDate O