e outlets. The firm generated 58% of its fiscal 2026 sales in the United States. \n\nMorningstar• yesterday\n- ### Deckers Earnings: Profitability Shines Despite Competitive Pressure; Shares Attractive\n\nFounded in 1973, California-based Deckers designs and sells casual and performance footwear, apparel, and accessories. In fiscal 2026, Ugg and Hoka accounted for 50% and 47% of total sales, respectively. Deckers also distributes a niche sandal brand Teva. Deckers produces most of its sales through wholesale partnerships but also operates e-commerce in more than 50 countries and has more than 200 company-operated stores, about half of which are outlets. The firm generated 58% of its fiscal 2026 sales in the United States. \n\nMorningstar• yesterday\n- ### UGG and HOKA brands show consistent growth\n\nDeckers Outdoor is a leading designer and seller of footwear and accessories for children, men, and women. Deckers sells its products through domestic and international retailers and directly to consumers through its websites and retail stores. Core brands include HOKA, UGG, Teva, and Ahnu. The company has 5,500 employees. The shares are a component of the S&P 500.\n\nArgus• 2 months ago","title":"Deckers Outdoor Corporation (DECK) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo Finance","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DECK/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DEO/","text":"Diageo plc (DEO) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo Finance\n\n# Diageo plc (DEO)\n\n95.97 -0.72 (-0.74%)\n\n At close: October 23 at 4:00:03 PM EDT \n\n95.97 0.00 (0.00%)\n\nAfter hours: October 23 at 4:00:27 PM EDT\n\n## Trading disclosure\n\n### 9.84%\n\n## Diageo plc Overview Beverages - Wineries & Distilleries / Consumer Defensive\n\nDiageo plc, together with its subsidiaries, engages in the production, marketing, and distribution of alcoholic beverages in North America, Europe, the Asia Pacific, Latin America and Caribbean, and Africa. It offers beer, scotch, gin, vodka, rum, liqueur, raki, wine, cachaça, tequila, brandy, and Chinese white spirit beverages, as well as Irish, Canadian, Chinese US, and Indian whisky. The company also provides ready-to-drink and non-alcoholic beverages. Its principal brands include Johnnie Walker, Don Julio, Guinness, Crown Royal, Smirnoff, Baileys, Captain Morgan, Buchanan's, Casamigos, Shui Jing Fang, and McDowell's. The company was formerly known as Guinness plc and changed its name to Diageo plc in February 1998. The company was incorporated in 1886 and is headquartered in London, the United Kingdom.\n\nwww.diageo.com \n\n27,972\n\n### Full Time Employees\n\nJune 30\n\n### Fiscal Year Ends\n\nConsumer Defensive \n\n### Sector\n\nBeverages - Wineries & Distilleries \n\n### Performance Overview\n\nTrailing total returns as of 10/23/2026, which may include dividends or other distributions. Benchmark is FTSE 100 (^FTSE) .\n\n### YTD Return\n\nDEO 13.39%\n\nFTSE 100 (^FTSE) 7.64%\n\n### 1-Year Return\n\nDEO 0.38%\n\nFTSE 100 (^FTSE) 11.61%\n\n### 3-Year Return\n\nDEO 30.66%\n\nFTSE 100 (^FTSE) 44.96%\n\n### 5-Year Return\n\nDEO 45.33%\n\nFTSE 100 (^FTSE) 48.38%\n\n### Earnings Per Share \n\nNo Earnings Per Share available for this ticker\n\n### Revenue vs. Earnings\n\nQ4 FY26\n\nRevenue 4.71B\n\nEarnings--\n\nProfit Margin 0.00%\n\nQ1\n\nFY23\n\nQ4\n\nFY25\n\nQ2\n\nFY26\n\nQ4\n\nFY26\n\n2B\n\n4B\n\n### Analyst Price Targets\n\n76.00 Low\n\n106.29 Average\n\n95.97 Current\n\n129.00 High\n\n### Analyst Recommendations\n\n Strong Buy Buy Hold Underperform Sell \n\n### Latest Rating\n\nDate 6/26/2026 Analyst TD Cowen Rating Action Upgrade Rating Buy Price Action Raises Price Target 88 -> 93\n\n- Market Cap \n- Enterprise Value \n- Trailing P/E \n- Forward P/E \n- PEG Ratio (5yr expected) \n- Price/Sales (ttm)\n- Price/Book (mrq)\n- Enterprise Value/Revenue \n- Enterprise Value/EBITDA \n\n#### Profitability and Income Statement\n\n- Profit Margin \n\n8.84%\n- Return on Assets (ttm)\n\n7.48%\n- Return o