s have mostly been bolt-on in nature, plugging gaps in the company’s product and geographic portfolio. \n\nMorningstar• 9 days ago\n- ### Plans to cut $850 million in costs over two years\n\nDiageo plc manufactures and markets alcoholic beverages worldwide. The company offers a variety of brands in the spirits, beer, cider, and wine categories. DEO's brands include Johnnie Walker, Crown Royal, J&B, and Windsor whiskies; Smirnoff, Ciroc, and Ketel One vodkas; and Captain Morgan, Don Julio, Tanqueray, and Guinness. Diageo plc was established in 1886 and is based in London.\n\nArgus• last month\n- ### The major stock indices are lower at midday. Data came out this morning that\n\nThe major stock indices are lower at midday. Data came out this morning that showed stubborn inflation on the wholesale side. Tomorrow, data will be released that will offer a view of inflation on the consumer side. Wall Street continues to monitor the price of oil and bond yields, both of which continue to creep higher. Crude oil is over $100 per barrel mark. The yield on the 10-year note is up nine basis points to 4.92%.\n\nArgus• last month\n- ### Diageo’s Turnaround Efforts Should Revive Growth, but the Road Is Long\n\nFormed in 1997 through the merger of Grand Metropolitan and Guinness, Diageo is the largest distiller globally by sales. Diageo acquired some of the Seagram assets in 2001, which gave it brands such as Captain Morgan rum and Crown Royal Canadian whisky. Since then, mergers and acquisitions have mostly been bolt-on in nature, plugging gaps in the company’s product and geographic portfolio. \n\nMorningstar• last month","title":"Diageo plc (DEO) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo Finance","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DEO/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/LVMUY/","text":"LVMH Moët Hennessy - Louis Vuitton, Société Européenne (LVMUY) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo Finance\n\n87.09 -0.32% \n\nOTC Markets OTCPK - Delayed Quote • U